  },
  {
    id: "urevo-strol-2e",
    name: "UREVO Strol 2E",
    brand: "UREVO",
    category: "Budget 2-in-1 Alternative",
    badge: "Cheapest Checked 2-in-1",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HG9D52DC?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ZS3Q+sfdL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$169.99 at UREVO (5 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":169.99,"high":169.99},
    specs: "0.6–6.2 mph with handle up · 265 lb capacity · about 15 x 40 in. belt · no incline",
    pros: [
      "UREVO and two hands-on reviews agree on the 265 lb rating and 6.2 mph",
      "A fold-down handle, like the UMAY U20F, for $40 less",
      "A one-year plus 180-day warranty",
    ],
    cons: [
      "No incline",
      "Sources give the belt as 40.1 or 40.2 inches long",
      "Narrow at 15 inches; walking speed is capped at 4 mph with the handle folded",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheaper, better-reviewed 2-in-1 to compare the U20F against if you do not need an incline.",
    description: "The Strol 2E is UREVO’s budget 2-in-1 walking pad with a handle that folds flat. UREVO’s US store listed it in stock at $169.99, against $289.99, on 5 November 2026, with 0.6 to 4.0 mph with the handle down and 0.6 to 6.2 mph with it raised, a 265 lb maximum load, a 2.25 HP maximum motor rating and a one-year plus 180-day warranty. Live Science and T3, both of which reviewed it hands-on, give the same 265 lb and 6.2 mph, which is more independent confirmation than any UMAY pad has. The belt is 40.2 inches long on UREVO’s page and 40.1 in other listings, which is why the card rounds.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Brands", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "UMAY Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/umay-treadmills/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are UMAY treadmills good?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "They are reasonable budget machines from a brand with its own US store, phone support and 30-day returns. Their figures need checking by model: the SF20 and L20 hold up against a second source, but the U20F walking pad carries 400, 300 and 265 lb weight limits across UMAY’s own pages.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the UMAY SF20?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "A folding treadmill with side handrails, a tablet holder and a three-position manual incline. On 5 November 2026 UMAY sold it at $289.99. UMAY and its manuals agree on a 400 lb capacity, a 3.0 HP motor rating and a 37.5 by 15-inch belt; the incline is 15% or 16% depending on the source.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Who makes UMAY treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "UMAY Fitness sells them from umayfitness.com and on Amazon but does not say who builds them. OCDevel’s walking-pad tracker reports that at least one UMAY pad is the same machine sold on Amazon as an ANCHEER, and describes UMAY’s pads as rebadged ANCHEER hardware.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What warranty does UMAY give?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On 5 November 2026 UMAY’s product pages gave one year on parts and one year on the structural frame for walking pads and treadmills, with a 30-day returns policy. A tracker recorded a five-year frame warranty earlier in 2026, so check the terms on the day you buy.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Has there been a UMAY treadmill recall?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "We searched the CPSC recall database for UMAY by title and manufacturer on 5 November 2026 and found no treadmill or walking-pad recall. Check your model number on the CPSC site before you buy, since marketplace products are sometimes recorded under another company’s name.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Where can I find UMAY treadmill reviews?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "UMAY’s own store shows buyer reviews, mostly positive, and Amazon shows more. We found no independent hands-on review of the SF20, U20F or L20. Read the low-star reviews for delivery damage and slow replacements, which are the complaints that recur.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 5,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/umay-treadmills/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/umay-treadmills/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "brands");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "umay treadmill",
      "umay fitness treadmill",
      "umay treadmill review",
      "umay sf20 foldable treadmill",
      "umay walking pad",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Most Searched UMAY: UMAY SF20 Foldable Treadmill", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Brand Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">UMAY Treadmills: What the Figures Really Say</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        UMAY Fitness sells budget walking pads and folding treadmills through its own US store and on Amazon, at sale prices that usually sit 40% below the “regular” price. We read every treadmill on UMAY’s store on 5 November 2026 and checked the main models against manuals and independent sources. Some figures hold up; others, including one weight limit, change from page to page.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#merach-novawalk-w50-trekpad"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41N86eQUrbL._SL500_.jpg" alt="MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#urevo-strol-2e"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ZS3Q+sfdL._SL500_.jpg" alt="UREVO Strol 2E" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad · UREVO Strol 2E</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          UMAY is one of the newer budget names in walking pads and folding treadmills: it has its own
          US web store with a phone number and a 30-day returns policy, sells on Amazon, and lists a
          wide range, from a $180 vibrating walking pad to a $600 treadmill with a 20% motorised incline.
          That is more than many marketplace brands offer. But UMAY’s own pages do not always agree with
          each other, independent reviews are thin, and the warranty is short. This guide covers the
          models people search for most, the SF20 above all, what we could confirm about each, and what
          to watch for before you buy.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Searched UMAY:</span> <a href="#umay-sf20">UMAY SF20 Foldable Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best UMAY Walking Pad:</span> <a href="#umay-u20f">UMAY U20F Folding 3-in-1 Walking Pad</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best UMAY for Heavier Users:</span> <a href="#umay-l20">UMAY L20 Foldable Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Checked Alternative:</span> <a href="#merach-novawalk-w50-trekpad">MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Cheapest Checked 2-in-1:</span> <a href="#urevo-strol-2e">UREVO Strol 2E</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we read the full product catalogue of UMAY Fitness’s US store
          (umayfitness.com, 44 products, including 14 walking pads and treadmills) with each model’s
          sale and “regular” price, stock status, description, warranty and returns terms, and read the
          SF20, U20F and Smart Walking Pad product pages and their buyer reviews in full. We
          cross-checked the SF20 against UMAY’s published manuals as indexed by a manuals site, the L20
          against its Best Buy marketplace listing title, and the brand against OCDevel’s walking-pad
          tracker. Amazon and Best Buy pages returned errors when we tried to read them, so we could not
          confirm Amazon prices or sellers. We found no hands-on review of the SF20, U20F or L20.
          Figures that conflict are stated as conflicts and kept off the cards. We searched the CPSC
          recall database for UMAY by title and manufacturer and found no treadmill recall. We have not
          tested any of these machines. Prices change often, and UMAY’s sale prices especially. We earn
          a commission if you buy through the Amazon links on this page; it does not change what we
          say.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">Are UMAY Treadmills Any Good? The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-is-umay">Who Makes UMAY Treadmills?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#models">UMAY Treadmills and Walking Pads: Our Picks</a></li>
            <li><a href="#umay-sf20">UMAY SF20 Foldable Treadmill: What We Could Confirm</a></li>
            <li><a href="#conflicts">Where UMAY’s Figures Disagree</a></li>
            <li><a href="#warranty-returns">UMAY Warranty, Returns and Support</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-should-buy">Who Should Buy a UMAY Treadmill</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Are UMAY Treadmills Any Good? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>UMAY treadmills are reasonable budget machines from a brand with its own US store,
            but their figures need checking model by model: the SF20 and L20 hold up against a second
            source, while the U20F walking pad carries three different weight limits across UMAY’s own
            pages.</strong> Buy one at the sale price, from UMAY’s store or a listing Amazon fulfils,
            assume the lowest weight limit you see, and do not count on the one-year warranty for much.
          </p>
          <p>
            What sets UMAY apart from most marketplace walking-pad names is that it exists outside the
            marketplace. UMAY Fitness runs a US web store with a phone line and support email, publishes
            a 30-day returns policy and free shipping over $49, and lists a range that runs from walking
            pads to <a href="/folding-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>folding treadmills</a>, ellipticals and bikes. That gives you somewhere to go if
            something goes wrong. Brands like <a href="/zofdim-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Zofdim</a>, which we could
            not trace at all, give you nothing of the kind.
          </p>
          <p>
            What UMAY does not give you is much independent evidence. We found no hands-on review of the
            SF20, U20F or L20. Our cards below therefore carry only the figures we could confirm against
            a manual or a second retailer, and say plainly where UMAY contradicts itself.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-is-umay" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Who Makes UMAY Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            UMAY sells as “Umay Fitness” from umayfitness.com, which replaced an older umayfit.com
            address. On 5 November 2026 its US store listed 44 products: 14 walking pads and treadmills,
            plus an elliptical, under-desk elliptical, exercise bikes, a <a href="/best-vibration-plates/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>vibration plate</a>, a
            stepper, Pilates boards, a home gym and accessories. It gives a US phone number and a support
            email, and its store prices are in US dollars with US shipping terms.
          </p>
          <p>
            Like most budget walking-pad brands, UMAY does not say who builds its machines. OCDevel’s
            walking-pad tracker, which reads Amazon listings and manuals, reports that at least one UMAY
            walking pad, the SM3, is the same machine sold on Amazon as an ANCHEER, with identical specs,
            and describes UMAY’s pads as rebadged ANCHEER hardware. We could not confirm that beyond the
            one model, but it is consistent with how this part of the market works: a small number of
            factories supply many labels. Our <a href="/ancheer-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">ANCHEER guide</a> covers that
            brand, and our <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">guide to buying a treadmill on Amazon</a> explains what it means for returns and support.
          </p>
          <p>
            UMAY also sells under names on Amazon that do not always match its own store. The SM3, for
            example, does not appear on UMAY’s site at all, and OCDevel found that the Amazon listing it
            had tracked for that model now shows a different product. Model names on UMAY’s store also
            shift: the U20F’s product address still reads U18F. If you are comparing a UMAY on Amazon with
            one on UMAY’s store, compare the photos, the <a href="/treadmill-belt-size-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>belt size</a> and the motor rating, not just the
            name.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="models" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>UMAY Treadmills and Walking Pads: Our Picks</h2>
<p>
            These are the three UMAY machines whose main figures we could check against a second source
            on 5 November 2026, plus two checked alternatives from other brands. Prices are UMAY’s sale
            prices on its own store on the day; UMAY shows every product at roughly 40% off a higher
            “regular” price, so treat the sale price as the real one. Where UMAY’s figures disagree with
            each other or with the manual, the figure is left off the card and the description says so.
          </p>
          <p>
            For handrails and a steep incline under $300, the SF20. For an under-desk walking pad with a
            handle and an incline, the U20F, with its weight limit treated cautiously. For a heavier user
            who wants a fuller treadmill, the L20. And if you want a weight limit and warranty you can lean
            on, the MERACH and UREVO cards are the comparison.
          </p>
        </div>
