          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Are UMAY treadmills good?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              They are reasonable budget machines from a brand with its own US store, phone support and 30-day returns. Their figures need checking by model: the SF20 and L20 hold up against a second source, but the U20F walking pad carries 400, 300 and 265 lb weight limits across UMAY’s own pages.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the UMAY SF20?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              A folding treadmill with side handrails, a tablet holder and a three-position manual incline. On 5 November 2026 UMAY sold it at $289.99. UMAY and its manuals agree on a 400 lb capacity, a 3.0 HP motor rating and a 37.5 by 15-inch belt; the incline is 15% or 16% depending on the source.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes UMAY treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              UMAY Fitness sells them from umayfitness.com and on Amazon but does not say who builds them. OCDevel’s walking-pad tracker reports that at least one UMAY pad is the same machine sold on Amazon as an ANCHEER, and describes UMAY’s pads as rebadged ANCHEER hardware.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does UMAY give?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 5 November 2026 UMAY’s product pages gave one year on parts and one year on the structural frame for walking pads and treadmills, with a 30-day returns policy. A tracker recorded a five-year frame warranty earlier in 2026, so check the terms on the day you buy.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Has there been a UMAY treadmill recall?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We searched the CPSC recall database for UMAY by title and manufacturer on 5 November 2026 and found no treadmill or walking-pad recall. Check your model number on the CPSC site before you buy, since marketplace products are sometimes recorded under another company’s name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where can I find UMAY treadmill reviews?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              UMAY’s own store shows buyer reviews, mostly positive, and Amazon shows more. We found no independent hands-on review of the SF20, U20F or L20. Read the low-star reviews for delivery damage and slow replacements, which are the complaints that recur.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

